00:01:57.880 --> 00:02:00.510
You woke him up by shoving a sword in his mouth?!

00:02:00.510 --> 00:02:02.010
Unbelievable!

00:02:02.010 --> 00:02:03.970
You could've seriously hurt him!

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:06.480
You see, Lim originally...

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:09.210
Hey, it's not a big deal. I can still eat, no problem—

00:02:09.210 --> 00:02:10.400
No, it <i>is</i> a big deal!

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:13.720
A-Anyway, what's going on?

00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:15.400
You're up so early this morning.

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:17.030
Y-Yeah...

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:20.720
I'm heading back to Zhcted's capital later today.

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:24.330
Before leaving, I wanted to ask what your plans are from here on out.

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:29.500
From here on out, huh?

00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:33.740
I'll come back the moment I've calmed down the king.

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:37.050
Hm, I need to take a guard detail with me.

00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:37.900
A hundred or so—

00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:39.260
Already taken care of.

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:40.760
Rurick will be leading them.

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:42.300
Oh, that's great!

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:45.420
What's wrong?

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:49.390
Lady Eleonora, where does your immense confidence in him come from?

00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:50.900
Confidence, huh?

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:53.150
For starters...

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:56.320
his power is absolutely fascinating.

00:02:57.240 --> 00:02:59.930
And I do like him somewhat.

00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:02.450
The same goes for you, doesn't it?

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:06.370
He has his merits, but I could never rely on him.

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:08.040
Sure, sure, I get it.

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:10.960
Just give him a hand, okay?

00:03:32.190 --> 00:03:34.730
Whoa, what's with that outfit?

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:38.030
You're about to visit Hunawihr, right?

00:03:38.030 --> 00:03:39.690
I'm going, too.

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:41.700
I even made lunch for us.

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:44.870
I want to see how the village is doing.

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:46.250
I won't have time for a picnic.

00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:47.910
I'm coming with you!

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:49.200
Titta...

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:50.710
With you!

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:55.170
Okay then.

00:03:55.170 --> 00:03:57.460
After all, what you went through is my fault.

00:03:57.460 --> 00:03:58.960
So why don't you come along?

00:04:00.170 --> 00:04:00.970
I'd love to!

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:04.970
Alsace was able to enjoy some peace and quiet

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:09.140
because both the Thenardier and Ganelon armies withdrew.

00:04:09.890 --> 00:04:12.480
Ultimately, that tranquility wouldn't last long.

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:15.480
Because the next move for the enemy forces would be...

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:20.530
Damn that Ganelon!

00:04:20.530 --> 00:04:23.780
The second my army had been defeated, he pulled back his own forces!

00:04:24.420 --> 00:04:26.970
And now he's waiting for my reaction.

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:30.080
So it seems.

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:33.240
When will the next dragon be ready?

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:35.040
In about a month.

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:41.090
What should we do about Count Vorn and the Zhcted war maiden?

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:44.440
We'll sick the Serrash on him.

00:04:44.440 --> 00:04:46.970
The notorious group of assassins?

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:49.100
He's as good as dead.

00:04:49.460 --> 00:04:53.480
As for the war maiden... 
we'll pit another war maiden against her!

00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:58.610
Are all of you fine?

00:04:58.610 --> 00:05:00.980
Yes, thanks to you, milord.

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:04.490
We hid in the woods, like we were told.

00:05:04.490 --> 00:05:07.200
They didn't notice us at all.

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:08.990
That's a load off my shoulders.

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:14.500
Meanwhile Elen went to Silesia, Zhcted's royal capital,

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:17.690
for an audience with King Viktor.

00:05:30.050 --> 00:05:31.640
Raise your head.

00:05:32.870 --> 00:05:37.540
Bearer of the Shining Demon Slayer, 
Eleonora Viltaria...

00:05:38.310 --> 00:05:45.040
We have heard you took an army into 
Brune territory without obtaining our permission.

00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:45.990
Is that true?

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:48.740
It is as you say, Your Majesty.

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:52.220
And why did you do such a thing?

00:05:52.220 --> 00:05:53.240
Tell me.

00:05:53.560 --> 00:06:00.000
I will determine a fitting punishment for that reckless conduct based on your response.

00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:04.010
I was hired to do so.

00:06:07.430 --> 00:06:09.800
What? Hired?

00:06:10.550 --> 00:06:11.550
By whom?

00:06:12.350 --> 00:06:14.770
By Count Tigrevurmud Vorn,

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:17.560
nobleman of Brune, and Lord of Alsace.

00:06:18.090 --> 00:06:18.770
I see.

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:23.570
So, what was this Count Vorn's objective? To take over the country?

00:06:24.180 --> 00:06:27.570
According to him, to protect the peace in Alsace.

00:06:28.900 --> 00:06:30.530
What a hollow excuse!

00:06:31.280 --> 00:06:33.370
Do you mean to involve our kingdom

00:06:33.370 --> 00:06:37.460
in a dangerous conflict by behaving like a common mercenary?!

00:06:38.660 --> 00:06:39.790
If I may...

00:06:46.090 --> 00:06:47.800
I would address Your Majesty.

00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:50.300
Sofya Obertas...

00:06:50.930 --> 00:06:56.680
Brune could not possibly want us involved in their internal conflict.

00:06:56.680 --> 00:07:00.190
They will inquire about Lady Viltaria's actions before long.

00:07:00.560 --> 00:07:04.440
When they do, we can explain what position our kingdom will take.

00:07:05.230 --> 00:07:10.810
And while her taking action without obtaining Your Majesty's leave is indeed an issue,

00:07:10.810 --> 00:07:15.410
battle has always favored haste over caution.

00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:29.090
My, my, of all the people to run into.

00:07:30.010 --> 00:07:33.720
To imagine you've started a war without permission...

00:07:38.640 --> 00:07:41.980
I see you still don't understand what your position as a war maiden entails,

00:07:41.980 --> 00:07:43.850
Eleonora Viltalia.

00:07:46.900 --> 00:07:50.270
And I see <i>you</i> are as tiny as ever,

00:07:50.270 --> 00:07:51.700
Ludmila Lourie.

00:07:53.110 --> 00:07:54.480
How about it?

00:07:54.480 --> 00:07:57.000
If you show some humility and bow your head,

00:07:57.000 --> 00:08:01.330
I'd gladly teach you how to grow a bit.
And I'm not only talking about your height.

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:02.620
Forget it.

00:08:03.160 --> 00:08:05.240
Nowadays you've got quite the mouth, haven't you?

00:08:05.240 --> 00:08:08.270
To think that you, the embodiment of boorishness and inelegance,

00:08:08.270 --> 00:08:10.220
would offer to teach others...

00:08:10.220 --> 00:08:12.050
Hear, hear...

00:08:16.970 --> 00:08:17.640
Geez,

00:08:18.390 --> 00:08:20.390
this won't do, you two.

00:08:21.120 --> 00:08:24.650
I'm always telling you to be nice to each other.

00:08:29.730 --> 00:08:30.910
She's the one who—

00:08:30.910 --> 00:08:32.030
No, <i>she</i> started it!

00:08:34.790 --> 00:08:36.220
By the way, Elen,

00:08:36.220 --> 00:08:38.160
why are you still here?

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:41.130
I was sure you would've already left the palace.

00:08:41.130 --> 00:08:42.290
Oh, right.

00:08:42.820 --> 00:08:44.210
Thank you, Sofy.

00:08:44.210 --> 00:08:46.920
You speaking up saved me.

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:50.010
I never would've caved in on my own.

00:08:50.010 --> 00:08:53.110
Caved in? That's a far cry from what happened, isn't it?

00:08:54.080 --> 00:08:56.220
I need to have an adult conversation with Sofy!

00:08:56.220 --> 00:08:57.450
Go away!

00:09:01.160 --> 00:09:02.930
Count Vorn, huh?

00:09:02.930 --> 00:09:06.100
One can only feel sorry for the poor guy having to put up with you.

00:09:09.190 --> 00:09:10.110
Elen,

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:14.400
one thing's for certain: 
you've turned Ludmila against you.

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:15.110
Huh?

00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:16.910
Mila—

00:09:16.910 --> 00:09:20.620
Ludmila has been in contact with Duke Thenardier for a long time.

00:09:20.950 --> 00:09:21.700
Huh?

00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:23.620
Her and Thenardier?!

00:09:23.620 --> 00:09:24.910
That's absurd!

00:09:24.910 --> 00:09:25.690
Indeed.

00:09:25.690 --> 00:09:29.750
She doesn't like Duke Thenardier's type at all.

00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:32.170
In fact, it's safe to say she hates him.

00:09:32.170 --> 00:09:33.130
Then why?

00:09:33.620 --> 00:09:38.120
Her family had been on good terms with 
House Thenardier long before she was even born.

00:09:38.870 --> 00:09:40.410
Do you think a girl as prim as her

00:09:40.410 --> 00:09:44.430
would ever let her personal feelings endanger such a partnership?

00:09:45.240 --> 00:09:49.560
You and Count Vorn have more enemies than only Duke Thenardier.

00:09:51.860 --> 00:09:53.910
Ludmila Lourie...

