00:10:04.580 --> 00:10:08.650
Lord Tigre! Lord Tigre!

00:10:09.570 --> 00:10:12.570
Lord Tigre, wake up!

00:10:13.910 --> 00:10:15.050
Lord Tigre!

00:10:33.720 --> 00:10:36.570
Come, till the ground.

00:10:46.500 --> 00:10:47.620
It hurts!

00:10:53.960 --> 00:10:55.460
Tigrevurmud...

00:10:58.710 --> 00:11:01.390
We are here in case something happens.

00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:05.180
We serve so that these people can live in peace.

00:11:05.180 --> 00:11:07.180
That's what feudal lords are for.

00:11:08.050 --> 00:11:09.180
Father...

00:11:09.980 --> 00:11:11.770
Tigrevurmud, you are...

00:11:11.770 --> 00:11:12.730
Father...

00:11:12.730 --> 00:11:13.980
Father...!

00:11:13.980 --> 00:11:15.730
Father!

00:11:16.730 --> 00:11:17.670
Father!

00:11:27.540 --> 00:11:28.450
Titta...

00:11:35.630 --> 00:11:37.000
Did you sleep well?

00:11:42.280 --> 00:11:43.770
I-I'm sorry!

00:11:43.770 --> 00:11:46.560
I was waiting for the right time to wake you up,

00:11:46.560 --> 00:11:47.810
but before I knew it...

00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:52.990
You must have been exhausted as well.

00:11:52.990 --> 00:11:54.150
Sorry.

00:11:54.610 --> 00:11:57.860
Don't be! I shouldn't have fallen asleep!

00:11:58.450 --> 00:11:59.420
Don't worry.

00:11:59.880 --> 00:12:01.950
Letting me rest helped me work something out.

00:12:03.720 --> 00:12:04.820
Great!

00:12:09.120 --> 00:12:12.830
It's a fine day for hunting.
Well, as long as nothing else happens.

00:12:16.720 --> 00:12:18.460
I'll come with you, wherever you go!

00:12:19.200 --> 00:12:22.590
You've helped me so much, Lord Tigre.

00:12:22.590 --> 00:12:25.640
Now it's my turn to lend you a hand.

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:27.640
Thanks.

00:12:28.180 --> 00:12:29.970
I'll have to keep moving as well.

00:12:32.230 --> 00:12:34.520
No, I <i>will</i> keep moving.

00:12:42.950 --> 00:12:43.990
That horse—

00:12:44.690 --> 00:12:46.160
Sir Mashas!

00:12:46.160 --> 00:12:47.870
He's back, isn't he?

00:12:48.950 --> 00:12:49.710
Yeah.

00:12:52.870 --> 00:12:53.660
Uh...

00:12:54.500 --> 00:12:55.750
Well then, Tigre,

00:12:56.210 --> 00:12:59.100
would you care to explain what's going on?

00:13:05.180 --> 00:13:07.130
Now I understand what has happened.

00:13:07.130 --> 00:13:08.570
Lady Limalisha,

00:13:08.570 --> 00:13:12.140
let me apologize for suspecting you and those under you.

00:13:12.600 --> 00:13:14.440
No, I should be the one to apologize.

00:13:14.440 --> 00:13:16.480
It was only natural to be cautious

00:13:16.480 --> 00:13:19.060
upon suddenly seeing soldiers from another kingdom here.

00:13:19.060 --> 00:13:24.030
Sir Mashas, I'm sorry to shock you right as you've come back.

00:13:24.030 --> 00:13:25.560
Don't worry about it.

00:13:25.560 --> 00:13:27.360
After all, nothing happened.

00:13:27.990 --> 00:13:29.450
Now then, Tigre...

00:13:29.450 --> 00:13:30.030
Yes?

00:13:31.580 --> 00:13:33.540
Let me hear your future plans.

00:13:38.830 --> 00:13:41.670
I'm going to attack Duke Thenardier.

00:13:47.560 --> 00:13:50.010
Then you're siding with Duke Ganelon?

00:13:50.470 --> 00:13:51.650
No.

00:13:51.650 --> 00:13:54.060
I have no plans to work with either of them.

00:13:54.790 --> 00:13:58.280
I trust you've given this a lot of thought beforehand.

00:14:00.080 --> 00:14:05.280
I inherited Alsace from my father. I have an obligation to defend it and the people living here.

00:14:05.670 --> 00:14:08.730
No, it's not because I have to.
I defend them because I want to.

00:14:09.300 --> 00:14:13.540
I'm a feudal lord.
I'm here to protect my subjects.

00:14:14.820 --> 00:14:20.580
Afterward, Mashas headed to the capital to have an audience with the King of Brune

00:14:20.580 --> 00:14:23.420
to make a case for Tigre's cause being just.

00:14:24.120 --> 00:14:29.590
In the meantime Tigre went from
county to county looking for allies.

00:14:35.060 --> 00:14:38.700
Thanks to Mashas, I have a general idea of what's happening.

00:14:39.440 --> 00:14:44.520
To be frank, I would've declined if the request came from you alone.

00:14:44.520 --> 00:14:46.620
Even though you may be in the right,

00:14:46.620 --> 00:14:49.520
you didn't stand a chance against Duke Thenardier before.

00:14:49.520 --> 00:14:50.610
Lord Augre!

00:14:51.990 --> 00:14:52.950
"Before"?

00:14:54.160 --> 00:14:55.040
Tigre...

00:14:55.440 --> 00:14:59.710
Or rather, Count Vorn, 
Mashas is no longer your only ally.

00:14:59.710 --> 00:15:04.250
The distinguished and powerful forces of Zhcted are also on your side.

00:15:04.820 --> 00:15:09.050
With them, you could go up against either Duke Thenardier or Duke Ganelon.

00:15:09.510 --> 00:15:10.790
Then will you help?

00:15:11.300 --> 00:15:13.220
You are on your way

00:15:13.220 --> 00:15:17.850
to becoming a third force, 
next to Thenardier and Ganelon.

00:15:18.480 --> 00:15:20.540
I swore allegiance to the royal family.

00:15:20.540 --> 00:15:23.360
I refuse to kowtow to one of the dukes.

00:15:24.120 --> 00:15:27.360
And I'm far from alone in thinking that.

00:15:33.570 --> 00:15:35.450
The mansion of Kikimora?

00:15:35.450 --> 00:15:38.500
A villa, just past the Vosges Mountains.

00:15:39.830 --> 00:15:41.370
Oh, you're here!

00:15:41.730 --> 00:15:42.920
Come, drink up!

00:15:44.400 --> 00:15:46.500
As of right now, I got the king's permission.

00:15:47.090 --> 00:15:49.850
However, it came with two caveats.

00:15:49.850 --> 00:15:52.840
If Alsace becomes my territory,

00:15:52.840 --> 00:15:55.390
I have to hand it over to the Kingdom of Zhcted.

00:15:55.970 --> 00:15:57.180
Hand over?

00:15:57.750 --> 00:16:00.020
You mean Alsace will be confiscated?

00:16:02.210 --> 00:16:05.310
Then again, that's only <i>if</i> it becomes her territory.

00:16:06.180 --> 00:16:08.730
The war has barely begun.

00:16:08.730 --> 00:16:11.030
There's several ways to change Alsace's situation.

00:16:11.990 --> 00:16:13.530
The real problem is the second condition.

00:16:14.400 --> 00:16:16.740
The king said this to me at the end:

00:16:17.410 --> 00:16:22.790
"Put the interests of Zhcted before anything else and behave prudently."

00:16:25.320 --> 00:16:27.040
Isn't that just a trite remark?

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:30.130
You don't get the point, do you?

00:16:30.130 --> 00:16:32.810
The crux of what His Majesty said

00:16:32.810 --> 00:16:36.350
is the part about putting our national interests first.

00:16:36.800 --> 00:16:37.600
Huh?

00:16:37.930 --> 00:16:41.800
Take, for example, a Zhcted nobleman with ties to Duke Thenardier.

00:16:41.800 --> 00:16:45.900
If they assert the duke's victory is in our king's best interest,

00:16:45.900 --> 00:16:47.810
they can take part in this war as they wish.

00:16:48.320 --> 00:16:50.110
They can't twist his words like that!

00:16:50.650 --> 00:16:54.490
The king deliberately phrased it to allow for such interpretations.

00:16:54.490 --> 00:16:57.240
He's making sure that all the parties involved are tied to him

00:16:57.240 --> 00:17:01.080
so that he benefits no matter who ends up as winner.

00:17:05.240 --> 00:17:06.580
A caretaker?

00:17:06.580 --> 00:17:07.960
I'll go see.

00:17:09.210 --> 00:17:10.140
Be that as it may,

00:17:10.140 --> 00:17:13.340
it's safe to assume the aristocrats won't make any sudden moves.

00:17:14.050 --> 00:17:17.590
There's a strict hierarchy in our kingdom. It starts with the king at the top,

00:17:17.590 --> 00:17:20.000
followed by the seven war maidens.

00:17:20.000 --> 00:17:21.850
The nobility is down below that.

00:17:22.560 --> 00:17:26.770
None of them has the power to oppose a war maiden head-on.

00:17:27.520 --> 00:17:28.520
Which means our problem...

00:17:29.480 --> 00:17:31.940
...is the other war maidens, right?

00:17:33.330 --> 00:17:35.760
Not all of them are on our side.

00:17:35.760 --> 00:17:37.740
But they're not our enemies either.

00:17:37.740 --> 00:17:39.870
At the moment, only one of them poses a risk to us.

00:17:40.640 --> 00:17:41.370
One of them?

00:17:41.910 --> 00:17:46.360
Whenever she opens her mouth, she goes on and on about good manners or character.

00:17:46.360 --> 00:17:49.630
And she looks like a potato that's just starting to put out shoots!

00:17:50.320 --> 00:17:52.130
Who're you calling a potato?!

00:17:53.050 --> 00:17:53.760
Lim!

00:17:53.760 --> 00:17:56.050
Why did you allow her to enter the mansion?!

00:17:56.840 --> 00:17:59.930
I hardly could have turned a war maiden away.

00:17:59.930 --> 00:18:01.260
A war maiden?

00:18:02.470 --> 00:18:04.850
Yes, one of the prized war maidens of Zhcted.

00:18:05.970 --> 00:18:09.350
I'm the Bearer of the Cleansing Spear, 
Ludmila Lourie.

00:18:10.310 --> 00:18:13.420
Pleased to meet you. Tigrevurmud Vorn.

00:18:14.610 --> 00:18:17.530
Tigre, this woman is not a guest.

00:18:17.530 --> 00:18:19.700
There's no need to extend your hospitality.

00:18:20.600 --> 00:18:23.390
Seems like my inkling to take a look in here was right.

00:18:23.390 --> 00:18:28.120
I've come to see you, Count Tigrevurmud Vorn.

00:18:28.600 --> 00:18:31.380
Let's take this conversation somewhere else.

00:18:38.120 --> 00:18:40.570
Why are you tagging along?

00:18:41.350 --> 00:18:43.720
You wanted a change of scenery, right?

00:18:43.720 --> 00:18:46.080
We're going to Rodnik.

00:18:46.080 --> 00:18:47.140
Tigre is coming with us.

00:18:47.730 --> 00:18:49.820
You're free to come with us.

00:18:52.230 --> 00:18:54.820
About what did you want to talk with me?

00:18:54.820 --> 00:18:58.700
Duke Thenardier has allies and partners outside of Brune.

00:18:59.610 --> 00:19:00.700
And I am one of them.

00:19:02.320 --> 00:19:04.200
You stand no chance against him.

00:19:06.870 --> 00:19:07.820
A trap?

00:19:11.920 --> 00:19:13.400
We're boxed in.

00:19:13.400 --> 00:19:15.210
Are they assassins?

00:19:18.630 --> 00:19:21.390
Bandits would've shown themselves almost immediately.

00:19:21.390 --> 00:19:23.890
So, which one of us are they after?

00:19:24.360 --> 00:19:25.140
You don't mean...?

00:19:25.680 --> 00:19:28.930
No. I'm the one who chose this road.

00:19:28.930 --> 00:19:32.100
They could very well be targeting Tigre.

00:19:32.100 --> 00:19:33.370
If he were to die here,

00:19:33.370 --> 00:19:36.570
Duke Thenardier and his bunch would dance for joy.

00:19:37.320 --> 00:19:40.400
Not to mention that I'd be forced to leave Brune.

00:19:40.400 --> 00:19:43.370
There's quite a few things I don't like about those prospects.

00:19:48.400 --> 00:19:49.200
He's about to shoot again!

00:20:00.380 --> 00:20:01.470
Serrash...?

00:20:15.900 --> 00:20:16.440
Lim!

00:20:23.620 --> 00:20:24.450
<i>With this species,</i>

00:20:25.120 --> 00:20:26.360
<i>she's got a chance.</i>

00:20:26.360 --> 00:20:28.950
<i>Once I suck out the poison, she'll survive.</i>

00:20:37.290 --> 00:20:37.920
Lim!

00:20:41.670 --> 00:20:42.630
Lavias!

00:20:54.690 --> 00:20:56.400
Cielo Zam Kafa!

00:21:17.880 --> 00:21:19.460
Are you done administering first aid?

00:21:23.090 --> 00:21:27.050
To think you'd get so flustered over one of your retainers...

00:21:27.700 --> 00:21:30.810
Eleonora, you are a failure as a war maiden.

00:21:32.680 --> 00:21:34.200
I'll go fetch a doctor.

00:21:35.640 --> 00:21:37.770
I'll meet you in Rodnik.

00:21:40.440 --> 00:21:41.360
Ludmila Lourie!

00:21:44.960 --> 00:21:47.240
Thank you for your help.

00:21:54.630 --> 00:21:55.720
She'll be fine.

